  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "notes": "Boot a Big Buck Hunter Pro ROM from an empty NVRAM and enter the S.A.M. switch test with the named Back and Select service keys (Back, then Select five times: service-menu splash, icon menu, diagnostics menu, switch menu, switch test). The scenario names no game, so one byte-identical file serves every bbh_* driver it is run against (bbh_160 and bbh_170). Every public switch starts at 0. Hold each matrix switch 1-64 in turn for 1.2 s with a snapshot while held, then release it for 0.6 s. The switch test prints the name the ROM gives a switch and marks it in its grid while the ROM reads it as active; the Avengers LE control scenario avs-switch-test-loki-control.json shows that this is the ROM's logical reading. The held addresses lie in the playfield matrix, outside every cabinet input the named keys drive.",
  "version": 1,
  "watch_switches": [
    21,
    22,
    34,
    37,
    43,
    45
  ]
